// Relay.xcconfig — where this build's documents come from, out of the box.
//
// The app is meant to work the moment it is installed: no folder to pick, no
// address to type. The address is committed here and included into every
// build (`App.xcconfig` includes this file unconditionally): it is only a
// hostname, and this repository is public, so it hides nothing the app bundle
// would not already reveal.
//
// PENCILLOOP_RELAY_URL has no scheme on purpose. An xcconfig treats `//` as the
// start of a comment, so `https://host` would silently become `https:` — a
// value that looks right in the file and is wrong in the build. The app puts
// the scheme back; it refuses anything that is not https anyway.
//
// The token is a credential and never goes in this file: the repository is
// public, and a committed token is read/write access to the documents for
// anyone who can read GitHub. It lives in Config/Local.xcconfig — copy
// Local.xcconfig.example — which is not committed and is included after this
// file, so it can override anything here. A checkout without it still builds
// and still knows the address; first run asks for the token instead of
// sliding silently into the folder transport.

PENCILLOOP_RELAY_URL = relay-production-49cf.up.railway.app
